@*
    Counter.razor — the canonical Blazor "Hello World": a single mutable int
    and a click handler. Key takeaways:

      • @page "/counter" makes this component routable at /counter.
      • @rendermode InteractiveServer opts THIS PAGE into server interactivity.
        Without it, the button would render as plain HTML and do nothing.
      • @onclick wires up a DOM event to a C# method. Blazor automatically
        calls StateHasChanged() after event handlers, so the UI re-renders
        on its own.
*@

@page "/counter"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Counter</PageTitle>

<h1>Counter</h1>

<p role="status">Current count: @currentCount</p>

<button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="IncrementCount">Click me</button>

@code {
    private int currentCount = 0;

    private void IncrementCount()
    {
        currentCount++;
    }
}
